 an independent  prosecutorial decision and if a charge  is brought  that the jury makes the key findings of  fact in this case  you know the blake family as you've  heard is asking that he  the officer rustin chesky be arrested  and charged what do you need to see to  bring charges against the officer  the charging decision in this case will  be made by a prosecutor  our office conducts the independent  investigation but  the standard for the use of deadly or  potentially deadly force  is if the officer reasonably believed  that the person against whom force was  used  was an imminent threat to the life or  to cause serious bodily harm to another  we want to gather the evidence as  fully and fairly but also swiftly  consistent with that as possible so that  a charging decision can be made  as quickly as possible in this case you  were one of the officials that  asked president trump not to come along  with the governor and the mayor of  kenosha but a lot of people were very  glad to see the president  his critics are calling it a photo op  others say it inflamed tensions there  what do you say about the president's  visit  well the situation on the ground in  kenosha had been improving significantly  over the past several days  and having the president come brought  more attention to that situation  we also unfortunately didn't hear any  condemnation of vigilante violence and  as the clip that you played earlier  indicated  there was nothing from the president  about how we can work  together to address systemic racism yeah  you talk about vigilante  let's talk about that for a second with  kyle rittenhouse there is a tape that  has just been released by his attorney  where kyle was asked if he wanted to  thank his fans which i think is an  interesting choice considering three  people were shot and two were dead  uh and he thanked them for overwhelming  support but does he have a case for  self-defense his attorney says this is a  watershed moment  is there a case 